{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "A Quick Coffee Break", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "And Then My Mother  Called", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 10, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe past experiences in a range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "packed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very crowded with people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The restaurant was packed for weekend brunch.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about health issues.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to jam up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to form a crowd in a limited space", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Customers jammed up the front desk of the restaurant all morning. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to perform", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go through the steps of doing a medical procedure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The doctors have performed some tests on my father.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be in the middle of ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in the process of doing a task", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was in the middle of keeping all the waiting customers under control, and then my mother called.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "crowd", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large gathering of people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There was a large crowd waiting at the front of the restaurant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "consequence", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the result of an action", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He used to eat a lot of deep-fried food, so now he has heart trouble as a consequence.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect and Past Simple Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way.<br><br>You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event not connected to the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use the Present Perfect, there is a connection between what happened in the past and now. You can use time markers like <span class=\"italic\"> for, just</span> or <span class=\"italic\"> ever</span> with the Present Perfect.<br><br>When you use the Simple Past tense, the time is always in the past. You can use time markers, like <span class=\"italic\">then, ago, yesterday, when I was</span>\u2026  <br><br>Look at the chart about how to form the Present Perfect tense:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Tense Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was / were\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has/have been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Your restaurant has always been popular.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to perform\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"performed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has/have performed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The doctors have performed some tests.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to see\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"saw\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has/have seen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I haven't seen her for a long time.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to catch\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"caught\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has/have caught\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The consequences have caught up with him.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Customers jammed up the front desk all morning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My mother called when I was in the middle of my work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My father ate a lot of deep-fried food.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Used to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Would</span> for Past Habits", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Would</span> and <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> have similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer.<br><br>However, there is an important difference between <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> does not require this.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Both <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span> are followed by a verb in the base form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> + verb<br><span class=\"italic\">My father used to take me to the park.</span<", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">would</span> + verb<br><span class=\"italic\">My grandfather and I would go to the library once a week, and he would help me pick out a book.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Used to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Customers used to come early in the morning.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They would line up outside even in the cold.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">My parents and I used to have regular visits.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They would come in to town once a week.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">My father used to eat a lot of dishes high in fat.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He would eat that for dinner almost every day.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Interview a family member one </br>generation older than you.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask them about new habits or routines they have started in the last year to improve their health.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the chart below to plan your questions and write your answers.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use used to and would to talk about what they used to do. Use the Present Perfect tense for new routines they have started. </br>(E.g., She used to eat junk food; now she has learned to cook healthy food.)<br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Questions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Answers\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "\ufffcI interview a family member about making a healthy change in their lifestyle.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I plan my questions in English in a table.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "\ufffcI record my information using words to express past habits and new routines.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about family life. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about people's past habits. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can discuss experiences I've had or haven't had.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Have you ever received surprising news? What was it?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you think you reacted in an appropriate way? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"c